---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const lastUpdated = "October 10, 2026";
// Meta measurement is described only when the pixel is configured at build time.
const metaPixelEnabled = /^\d{5,20}$/.test((import.meta.env.PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID || "").trim());
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Practice Startup Services collects, uses, and protects your information."
  noIndex={false}
>
  <section class="border-b border-ink/8 py-14 lg:py-20 relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10 opacity-[0.04]" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg width="100%" height="100%" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <defs>
          <pattern id="bp-grid-priv" x="0" y="0" width="48" height="48" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
            <path d="M 48 0 L 0 0 0 48" fill="none" stroke="hsl(var(--ink-800))" stroke-width="1" />
          </pattern>
        </defs>
        <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#bp-grid-priv)" />
      </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="container-site relative">
      <div class="max-w-prose mx-auto">
        <div class="phase-label text-bronze-700 mb-5">Legal</div>
        <h1 class="font-display text-display-xl font-medium text-ink mb-3 text-balance">
          Privacy Policy.
        </h1>
        <p class="font-mono text-label text-graphite-600 tracking-[0.18em] uppercase">
          Last updated: {lastUpdated}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 lg:py-20">
    <div class="container-site">
      <div class="prose-editorial">
        <p class="text-lede text-graphite-800 leading-relaxed mb-8 text-pretty">
          Practice Startup Services ("we," "us") respects your privacy. This policy explains what
          information we collect when you use practicestartupservices.com, how we use it, and the
          choices you have. We keep this short and honest.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect.</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Information you give us.</strong> When you schedule a consultation, fill out a
          form, or contact us by email, we collect the information you provide, typically your
          name, email address, phone number, professional role, target launch timing, and a short
          description of what you're working on. We use this to respond to you and to prepare for
          the consultation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Information we collect automatically.</strong> Like most websites, we collect
          basic technical information when you visit: browser type, device, referring URL, pages
          viewed, time spent. We use this to understand what's working and to improve the site.
          We do not sell this information. It may be processed by the service providers described below.
        </p>
        <h2>Free planning tools and registration.</h2>
        <p>Your checklist and pro forma are saved in your browser. Their downloads are created on your device. We do not receive the notes, task owners, or financial inputs through the LaborGenie registration form. Clearing your browser data removes the saved plans; use the download or backup controls to keep a copy.</p>
        <p>If you register for the free LaborGenie license offer, we collect your email and practice name through HubSpot, our customer relationship management provider. We use them to record your request and contact you about access. Your submission also includes the form and page context and the preferences you select. License access is arranged by PPS; submitting the form does not automatically activate an account.</p>
        <p>You can separately choose marketing emails from PPS about startup resources and products, including the upcoming EHR, LaborGenie, and UnfairCPA. This choice is optional and is not required to request the license. You can unsubscribe from marketing emails at any time. No signup on this site creates an UnfairCPA account.</p>

        <h2>Free startup research.</h2>
        <p><strong>Free preview.</strong> When you run the research preview, your provider type, specialty, ZIP code, practice model, care setting, payment model and launch stage are sent to our server to look up public data from the CMS NPI Registry and the U.S. Census Bureau. No email is needed. We cache the public data we retrieve; the cache contains no personal information.</p>
        <p><strong>Written brief.</strong> If you request the written brief, your email address goes to PPS through HubSpot, together with the page address, any campaign tags described below, and the practice details you selected (when our form is set up to receive them). We use it to record your request and so a startup specialist can follow up about it. Optional marketing emails are a separate choice and are not required for the brief. Your practice details and the public facts shown on the page (not your email) are sent to OpenAI, our AI provider, to write the brief. A Cloudflare Turnstile check helps prevent automated abuse. To prevent duplicate requests and enforce daily limits, we store a one-way hashed form of your email and IP address and a copy of the brief you received. The brief appears on the page and in a PDF you download; this site does not send automated emails.</p>

        <h2>Campaign attribution.</h2>
        <p>If you arrive from an ad or a link with campaign tags (such as utm_source or an ad click identifier), we store those tags, the page you landed on, and the address of the site that referred you in your browser. The first visit is kept for up to 90 days and the most recent for your browser session. They are sent with any request you submit so we know which campaign brought you. We never send what you type into forms or planners to analytics or advertising tools.</p>
        {metaPixelEnabled && (
          <>
            <h2>Meta measurement.</h2>
            <p>We use the Meta Pixel to measure how our Instagram and Facebook ads perform. For every visitor, the pixel sends Meta the page address (including any campaign tags in it), the referring page, your IP address, browser and device information, and Meta cookie identifiers. It records page views and, when you successfully request a research brief, a lead event. When you request a brief, our server may also send Meta that lead event with your IP address, browser user agent and Meta cookie identifiers so the two can be matched. We do not intentionally send your email address, phone number, or anything you type to Meta, and our Meta settings are configured not to collect form contents automatically. You can manage ad preferences in your Meta account settings.</p>
          </>
        )}

        <h2>What we don't collect.</h2>
        <p>
          We do not collect or store any protected health information (PHI). This site is for
          practice operators, not patients. If you accidentally include PHI in a form or
          conversation, we ask you to redact it and we will delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use what we collect.</h2>
        <p>
          We use your information to respond to your inquiry, schedule and prepare for your
          consultation, send follow-up communications if you opt in, and improve the site and our
          services. We do not sell your information to third parties.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use a small number of service providers to operate the site (hosting, email delivery,
          CRM, analytics, and an AI provider for the optional research brief). Each provider has access only to the information they need to do their
          job and is bound by their own confidentiality terms.
        </p>

        <h2>How we protect what we collect.</h2>
        <p>
          We use industry-standard security practices including encryption in transit (TLS),
          encryption at rest where applicable, access controls, and routine audits. No system is
          perfectly secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security. We will notify you
          promptly if a breach affects your information.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices.</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us to:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-body text-graphite-800 leading-relaxed space-y-1 mb-5">
          <li>Tell you what information we have about you</li>
          <li>Correct inaccurate information</li>
          <li>Delete your information from our records</li>
          <li>Stop sending you marketing communications</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Email <a href="mailto:hello@practicestartupservices.com" class="underline text-ink hover:text-bronze-700">hello@practicestartupservices.com</a> with any of these requests.
          We respond within 30 days.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies.</h2>
        <p>
          We use a small number of cookies: one to maintain your visitor session on the site,
          and a small set used by our hosting provider (Cloudflare) for performance and security.
          Our site includes Google Analytics and Google Ads measurement{metaPixelEnabled ? ", and Meta Pixel measurement" : ""}. The registration form also uses HubSpot and its spam-prevention service, and the research brief form uses Cloudflare Turnstile. These providers may use cookies or similar technologies for measurement, form delivery, and spam prevention.
        </p>

        <h2>Children.</h2>
        <p>
          This site is intended for medical professionals planning a practice. It is not directed
          at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect information from children.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy.</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy as our practices evolve. The "Last updated" date at the top
          reflects the most recent version. Material changes will be noted on the home page or
          via email if you've shared one with us.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact.</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:hello@practicestartupservices.com" class="underline text-ink hover:text-bronze-700">hello@practicestartupservices.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
